# HTML Structure — ZatPat IMS

## Single File SPA

Everything lives in `index.html`. No routing library — view switching is done by adding/removing the `hidden` class on `<section class="view" id="view-{name}">` elements.

## Structure

```
<body>
  #auth-screen          — login/signup forms + demo buttons
  #app                  — the main app shell (hidden until authenticated)
    #sidebar            — desktop nav with grouped links
    #sidebar-overlay    — backdrop for mobile sidebar
    .topbar             — page title, search, theme toggle, notifications, user avatar
    .main-content       — contains all <section class="view"> elements
    #bottom-nav         — mobile-only bottom navigation (5 tabs)
    .more-sheet-overlay — backdrop for mobile "More" sheet
    .more-sheet         — slide-up menu for secondary nav items on mobile
  Modals                — positioned fixed, toggled via `hidden` class
  #toast-container      — bottom-right toast notifications
  #delete-modal         — shared confirmation dialog (reused by all modules)
```

## Adding a New View

1. Add a `<section class="view hidden" id="view-{name}">` inside `.main-content`
2. Add a nav item in `#sidebar` with `data-view="{name}"`
3. Add the route in `App._navigate()` (`titles` map + call module's render/refresh)
4. If it's a primary mobile view, add a `<button class="bnav-item" data-view="{name}">` to `#bottom-nav`; otherwise add it to `.more-sheet`
5. Update `_syncBottomNav()` if it's a primary view

## Adding a New Modal

- Use the existing pattern: `<div class="modal hidden" id="{name}-modal">`
- Include `.modal-overlay` + `.modal-content` + `.modal-close` button
- Open by removing `hidden`, close via the shared `_bindModalClose()` handler in `app.js`

## Script Load Order

Scripts are loaded at the bottom of `<body>` in dependency order:
`store.js` → `auth.js` → `locations.js` → `products.js` → `inventory.js` → `orders.js` → `shop.js` → `pos.js` → `bom.js` → `khata.js` → `reports.js` → `dashboard.js` → `export.js` → `app.js`

`app.js` must be last — it calls `App.init()` on `DOMContentLoaded`.
